        "IQS_06": {
            "question_id": "IQS_06",
            "status": "scored",
            "score": 5,
            "description": "MongoDB's competitive position is moderately稳固 but visibly deteriorating. Strengths: Named Gartner Magic Quadrant Leader for Cloud DBMS (4th consecutive year, Nov 2025); Atlas revenue grew 30% YoY (Q3 FY2026), reaching ~$2B run-rate; 68,000+ customers; 40% of Fortune 100; strong developer mindshare; multi-cloud differentiation across AWS/Azure/GCP; AI positioning via Voyage AI acquisition. Weaknesses/Erosion: MongoDB Enterprise Advanced mindshare fell from 23.3% to 16.9% YoY in Managed NoSQL — a significant erosion; in Aug-Sep 2025, Microsoft donated DocumentDB to Linux Foundation with backing from AWS, Google Cloud, and Snowflake, creating a unified vendor-neutral open-source front; Azure Cosmos DB (16.8% mindshare) and AWS DocumentDB (8.1%) directly compete; gross margin compressed from 75% to 73%; MongoDB holds only ~2% of the $100B total DBMS market; pricing pressure intensifying in maturing DBaaS market. Verdict: Position is still defensible as the independent multi-cloud document database leader, but the trend clearly supports deterioration rather than enhancement or stability, so the score sits at the middle.",
